⍝ Run the Jarvis WebSocket tests from the shell:
⍝     dyalogscript Tests/WebSockets/run.apls
⍝ Loads Source/Jarvis.dyalog (relative to this script) unless JARVIS_SOURCE names another copy,
⍝ uses ports from JARVIS_TEST_PORT (default 8291) up, runs #.test_WebSockets.Run, prints any failures, and exits with 0 if every test passed, 1 otherwise.
⎕IO←1
here←{⊃1 ⎕NPARTS ⍵}⊃{⍵/⍨∨/¨'run.apls'∘⍷¨⍵}2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs'
src←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'JARVIS_SOURCE'
src←(1+0∊⍴src)⊃src(here,'../../Source/Jarvis.dyalog')
⎕←'Jarvis source: ',src
{}#.⎕FIX'file://',src
{}#.⎕FIX'file://',here,'test_WebSockets.apln'
{0∊⍴⍵:⍬ ⋄ #.test_WebSockets.BasePort←¯1+⊃⊃(//)⎕VFI ⍵}2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'JARVIS_TEST_PORT' ⍝ first port to use
failures←#.test_WebSockets.Run
⎕←''
⎕←(⍕≢failures),' failure(s)'
⎕←⍪failures
⎕OFF(0≠≢failures)
